# The session image's build context. The Dockerfile's build stage does
# `COPY . .` to compile sessiond, so everything reachable from here lands in a
# layer of the intermediate image; what is excluded is excluded because it is
# either large, machine-local, or something that must never be near an image.
#
# Nothing here is a security control on its own — the final stage copies exactly
# one file out of the build stage — but a context that carries a developer's
# worktrees, binaries and logs makes the build slower and the layers harder to
# reason about, and `.git` in particular carries every branch of the repository
# into a build that needs none of it.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
bin/
artifacts/
*.log
docs/
assets/
